        "content": "Documents give contradicting answers about the same thing. Other documents, which take no side, may state a fact that makes one of the answers impossible.\n\nQuestion: What is the population of Washington Township, Michigan?\n\nAnswer A: 1,500\n  about: Washington Township, Michigan\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: 2000\n  kind: factual\n  attributed to: census\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"As of the census [1] of 2000, there were 1,500 people, 335 households, and 268 families residing in the township.\" [document 4]\n\nAnswer B: 1,636\n  about: Washington Township, Michigan\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: 2000\n  kind: factual\n  attributed to: census\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"As of the census of 2000, there were 1,636 people, 610 households, and 477 families residing in the township.\" [document 7]; \"As of the census of 2000, there were 1,636 people, 610 households, and 477 families residing in the township.\" [document 8]\n\nThe other documents:\nDocument 1: Washington Township, Gratiot County, Michigan Washington Township is a civil township of Gratiot County in the U.S. state of Michigan. The population was 909 at the 2000 census. According to the United States Census Bureau, the township has a total area of , of which is land and (0.08%) is water. As of the census of 2000, there were 909 people, 335 households, and 268 families residing in the township. The population density was 25.6 per square mile (9.9/km²). There were 352 housing units at an average density of 9.9 per square mile (3.8/km²). The racial makeup of the township\nDocument 2: ) is land and 0.04 square miles ( 0.10 km 2 ) ( 0.08 % ) is water . The township contains portions of the Maple River State Game Area . Demographics [ edit ] As of the census [ 1 ] of 2000 , there were 909 people , 335 households , and 268 families residing in the township . The population density was 25.6 per square mile ( 9.9/km 2 ) . There were 352 housing units at an average density of 9.9 per square mile ( 3.8/km 2 ) . The racial makeup of the township was\nDocument 3: Washington Township , Gratiot County , Michigan - Academic Kids Washington Township , Gratiot County , Michigan Washington Township is a township located in Gratiot County in the U.S. state of Michigan . As of the 2000 census , the township had a total population of 909 . Geography According to the United States Census Bureau , the township has a total area of 91.9 km² ( 35.5 mi² ) . 91.8 km² ( 35.4 mi² ) of it is land and 0.1 km² ( 0.04 mi² ) of it is water . The total area is 0.08 % water\nDocument 5: a few degrees cooler allowing for more snow in the winter. A notable weather event occurred on July 2, 1997 when, during the Michigan Tornado Outbreak, a EF0 tornado touched down at 26 mile Road and destroyed parts of the Rudgate trailer park community. Six people were injured during the events. As of the census of 2010, there were 25,139 people (up from 19,080 in 2000), 9,258 households, and 7,160 families residing in the township. The population density was 699.2 per square mile (270.0/km²). There were 9,258 occupied housing units and 612 vacant units. The racial makeup of the township\nDocument 6: ( s ) 248 and 586 FIPS code 26-84120 GNIS feature ID 1627216 Washington Charter Township , located within Metro Detroit , is a charter township of Macomb County in the U.S. state of Michigan . The population was 28,165 at the 2020 census , up from 25,139 in 2010 . Contents History Geography Communities Weather Demographics History Washington Township was organized in 1827 . It is home to the historic Octagon House , built by Loren Andrus from 1858 to 1860 . Westview Orchards was founded in what is now Washington Township in 1813 . The Mount Vernon Cemetery\n\nLook in the other documents for a fact that rules one answer out: a date of birth that makes a person too young, for example, or a plain statement that the answer is false. Use only what these documents say, nothing you know from elsewhere. A fact that only makes an answer less likely does not count.\n\nReply with JSON only. If such a fact is there:\n{\"reason\": \"one sentence\", \"impossible\": \"A\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\"}\n\"impossible\" is the letter of the answer that is ruled out. \"quote\" is the sentence stating the fact, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in.\nIf there is none:\n{\"impossible\": null}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
